; Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
;
; windows-win32-shim export manifest — the single source of truth for the set of
; `m<Name>` entry points the shim DLL exports, and the input to the alias
; generator (`alias_gen`, MW5-2) that mirrors the C++ `generate_mwin32_alias.cmake`.
;
; Parity target: the C++ `mwin32.def`. Every genuine Win32 registry / filesystem
; name has an `m<Name>` shim spelling here. A name is ACTIVE (uncommented) only
; when this crate actually exports that symbol today — either a real W-form
; implementation or a `NOT_SUPPORTED` stub. Names this crate does NOT yet export
; are present but COMMENTED OUT with a leading `;`; enable one by simply deleting
; its leading `;` once the entry point lands (e.g. the ANSI `A` forms in MW6).
; Keeping the full roster here means the manifest never has to be re-derived.
;
; The `.def` comment marker is `;` (comment to end of line). A leading `;` thus
; disables the whole line; a trailing `; noalias` keeps the name exported but
; opts it OUT of auto-redirection (see `mCloseHandle` — redirecting every
; `CloseHandle` in a client would capture non-shim OS handles). See SHIM-D4.
;
; Changing the ACTIVE set is a breaking change for any consumer linking the
; generated alias object.

